# Architecture: Service Layer

- A service must represent one isolated capability or integration.
- Service interfaces must live in `app/modules/<module>/domain/services.py`.
- Technical service implementations must live in `app/modules/<module>/infrastructure`.
- Services may generate tokens, hash passwords, send emails, send notifications, upload files, integrate with external APIs, work with payment providers, or work with AI providers.
- Service interfaces must end with `Service`, `Provider`, `Client`, or `Hasher`.
- Keep each service focused on one technical, operational, or domain capability.
- Do not let a service orchestrate a complete business workflow.
- Do not let a service replace a use case.
- Do not put endpoint-specific HTTP behavior or response-schema construction inside services.
